      "writtenOn": "2022-08-30T18:12:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a bit of a shift, and we can change back to preserving the inter-pipeline batching/sharing of data.\n\nThe main reason for this change was to reduce how much information we needed to provide at track and lookup/bind time, and reduce the complexity of those lookups. So this switches from a hash-map lookup to an array access.\n\nAssuming that there aren\u0027t that many pipelines and not that many duplicate references to data, this is probably a reasonable trade off for a little bit more GPU memory transfer but faster tracking/recording on the CPU.\n\nWe should be able to go back to the batch system by changing these SkTArrays to SkTHashMaps that take a batch key. We can keep the pipeline index -\u003e batch key lookup external to DrawPassUniformWriter because DrawPass::Make has access to `drawPass-\u003efPipelineDescs[index]` from which we can get to the render step unique ID or the paint ID depending on usage.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 302,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 302,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "1c59ba9a13247de0cb19ecb6e0991dc53dc297cc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
